    "lawCode": "Amd §911, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4880\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to adding the Onondaga\ncreek to the definition of \"inland waterway\" for the purposes of\nwaterfront revitalization\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nThis bill would designate Onondaga Creek as an inland waterway.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nAmends subdivision 4 of section 911 of the executive law by adding\nOnondaga Creek to the list of water bodies defined as inland\nwaterways.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThis bill would designate Onondaga Creek as an inland waterway thus\nmaking the municipalities and organizations along its banks eligible\nfor funding from the Department of State and Environmental Protection\nFund waterfront revitalization grants program. The ability to apply\nfor and receive this grant funding is of considerable importance to\nincreasing the opportunities for these creekside communities.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
